  "claim_scope": "v5 re-pin (C4a): the canonical manifest checker and its test record the ten certificate serializers and four certificate enums (102 serializers, 34 enums, 219 hash_global_v1 calls, 93 call files, 94 closure files); guard sources unchanged. v4 re-issue (Codex C1'' P2): the reserve-counting mutation is attributed to the behavioural vector that fails under it (the column-name test stays green when reserves are folded into the existing custody column); pins unchanged. Append-only correction after the Opus C2-prime review: every implementation mutation now names the vector replay node that fails under it (the polarity test only backs the declared-polarity mutation), the two overflow killers are stated against the one shared fold helper, and the O-008 replay executes both golden replays. Earlier: re-pin after candidate C2-prime repaired the Opus C2 review findings: the custody fold overflow is reachable (GlobalEconomicStateV1 validates rows, not supply equality) and is now pinned by the vector rejects_custody_aggregate_overflow; the composed guard has, since source commit 85c45bd629f6793e06d995a335ec92fc8a5926e6, folded all four tables before evaluating any inequality, so a state whose OPEN-terminal fold overflows and whose entitlements exceed same-domain custody reports CLAIMANT_BACKING_TOTAL_OVERFLOW where the pre-C2 guard reported LIABILITIES_EXCEED_SAME_CONTROL_DOMAIN_BACKING (both fail closed); the mutation-killer table now declares and checks each killer's expected outcome code; the Rust view is validated by a checked constructor. Research-only source-bound evidence that the state-visible necessary claimant-backing checks of the global economic refinement fold exactly custody, claimant-entitlement, and OPEN-terminal totals into a typed ClaimantBackingViewV1 with no reserve or balance column, reject through a closed three-code enum with fixed precedence and byte-identical messages in Python and Rust, and are bound across both languages by one rendered golden vector; and that the accounting source classification contract pins the normative partition and the V1 alias table without renaming any wire field.",
